  "description": "IFIPAR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C100 H70 F30 La4 O26,C1 H1 Cl3,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La4 (La) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.078-4.238 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.70-115.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [La4(BTFA)10(μ3-OH)2(H2O)4]·4(H2O)·(CHCl3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
